From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: qatcod <79017227+qatcod@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 00:30:53 +0500
Subject: [PATCH] 9573: #6205 Put the MCS-96 division quotient in the low word

DIV, DIVB, DIVU and DIVUB all wrote the result as

    lreg = zext(div:2 << 16) | rem;

which is wrong twice over. The quotient and remainder are the wrong way
round: the MCS-96 puts the quotient in the low half of the destination and
the remainder in the high half. And the shift is evaluated at the width of
`div:2`, so shifting a two byte value left by 16 discards every bit of it.
The destination ended up holding the remainder alone, which is why the
decompiler showed a modulo where the program divides.

Widen before shifting and swap the halves, so the quotient lands in the low
half and survives. DIVB and DIVUB had the same shape at byte width.
---
 Ghidra/Processors/MCS96/data/languages/MCS96.sinc | 8 ++++----
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Ghidra/Processors/MCS96/data/languages/MCS96.sinc b/Ghidra/Processors/MCS96/data/languages/MCS96.sinc
index 008f410179..e7bfedc1a8 100644
--- a/Ghidra/Processors/MCS96/data/languages/MCS96.sinc
+++ b/Ghidra/Processors/MCS96/data/languages/MCS96.sinc
@@ -645,7 +645,7 @@ macro setSignedShiftRightCarryFlag(shiftee,amount) {
 	local den = oper16;
 	local div = num s/ sext(den);
 	local rem = num s% sext(den);
-	lreg = zext(div:2 << 16) | rem;
+	lreg = (zext(rem:2) << 16) | zext(div:2);
 @if defined(C196KB) || defined(C196KC)
 	$(V) = ((div s> 0x7fff) | (div s< 0x8001));
 @endif
@@ -657,7 +657,7 @@ macro setSignedShiftRightCarryFlag(shiftee,amount) {
 	local den = oper8;
 	local div = num s/ sext(den);
 	local rem = num s% sext(den);
-	wreg = zext(div:1 << 8) | rem;
+	wreg = (zext(rem:1) << 8) | zext(div:1);
 @if defined(C196KB) || defined(C196KC)
 	$(V) = ((div s> 0x7f) | (div s< 0x81));
 @endif
@@ -669,7 +669,7 @@ macro setSignedShiftRightCarryFlag(shiftee,amount) {
 	local den = oper16;
 	local div = num / zext(den);
 	local rem = num % zext(den);
-	lreg = zext(div:2 << 16) | rem;
+	lreg = (zext(rem:2) << 16) | zext(div:2);
 	$(V) = (div > 0xffff);
 	$(VT) = $(VT) | $(V);
 }
@@ -679,7 +679,7 @@ macro setSignedShiftRightCarryFlag(shiftee,amount) {
 	local den = oper8;
 	local div = num / zext(den);
 	local rem = num % zext(den);
-	wreg = zext(div:1 << 8) | rem;
+	wreg = (zext(rem:1) << 8) | zext(div:1);
 	$(V) = (div > 0xff);
 	$(VT) = $(VT) | $(V);
 }
